Role & Feature Matrix
1. Student Portal
 * Browse Programmes: View course details, requirements, and information without barrier.
 * Submit Application: Fill out the cycle-specific form, choose courses, and upload required documents.
 * Email Confirmation: Receive automatic email confirmation containing their generated Application Number and their own created PIN.
 * Status Dashboard: Log in using their Application Number and PIN to view overall status, submitted details, and uploaded files.
 * Document Re-upload: Restricted re-upload access triggered only if an admin flags and rejects a specific document with a specified reason.
 * Outcome Notifications: Receive automated acceptance letters or rejection notices via email.
 * Offer Management: Accept or reject course admission offers within a specified deadline.
2. Administrator Portal
 * Cycle Management: Create, configure (dates, qualification types, available courses, custom form fields), and publish application cycles.
 * Application Review: Access cycle-specific dashboards to view applicant forms and submitted documents.
 * Manual Decision Engine: Manually evaluate applicants against institutional selection criteria and update admission statuses based on space availability and document validity.
 * Audit Trail: View personal administrative activity history for transparency and tracking.
3. Academic Head Portal
 * Full Administrative Access: Inherits all base Admin privileges.
 * User Management & Access Control: View all registered admin accounts, monitor activity, and enable or disable access permissions per admin.
 * Data Export: Export complete application forms and supporting document packages per intake cycle.
 * Billing Management: Pay Atlas platform licensing fees for the institution.
